## 2. Cooperation Model

How the two-player dependency is enforced. _(TBD — pick a primary model)_

Candidate models:
- **Asymmetric roles** — each player has distinct abilities (e.g. one moves blocks, one phases through walls).
- **Symmetric + shared mechanics** — identical players, but obstacles need two bodies (co-op switches, boosting, catching).
- **Hybrid** — mostly symmetric with a few role-defining tools.

