2. **Local or online co-op** — or both? Strongly shapes the tech.
3. **Camera** — shared single screen (forces players to stay together) or split?
4. **Tone & setting** — comedic, tense, cozy? What world?
5. **Failure rules** — shared lives, checkpoints, who-resets-on-death?
6. **Level length** — "one long level" = roughly how many minutes of play?
7. **Tech stack / engine** — and target platform(s).
8. **Communication assumption** — same couch (voice) or remote (need in-game signaling)?
